const e="texas-4h-talent-showcase",u=2026,t="Combines District 11 (2025-26, newest) and District 5/4 (2023). Where they differ the page says which district. Not printed: ages of divisions, entry fees, event dates, venues, marks per criterion, prizes. The District 11 document prints contact emails and phones of its two contest directors (Extension staff); these are kept as contact variables. The Google Drive music folder is a public link.",n={Title:"Rules & Criteria",Subtitle:"Texas 4-H Talent Showcase (formerly Share-the-Fun). Read these rules before you register.",NoticeTitle:"Please Read Before Registering",Notice:"Choose the correct category when you register. Entering the wrong category may result in disqualification. Time limits are strictly enforced.",Notes:["Questions on Vocal, Instrumental Music and Solo/Band Performance: {{VocalContact}}.","Questions on Choreographed Routines, Variety Show, 4-H Skit and Poetry/Prose: {{StageContact}}."],Sections:[{Key:"general",Title:"General Rules",Items:["The Talent Showcase is a competitive event of the Theater and Performance Arts project (District 5/4 rules).","Objectives: develop a spirit of cooperation by working together; build self-confidence through public appearance; encourage a broad recreation program in 4-H at club and county level; help members discover and develop their talents; support social, cultural and leadership development.","There are seven categories, each with its own description and score card. The score cards are in the state guidelines at {{StateGuidelinesLink}}.","The state guidelines are written for the senior contest at State Round-Up. The district contest details are in the district document.","Participants must compete with the same material at county, district and state level. For example, you cannot change songs between district and state.","Acts may fine-tune a performance after the county and district critiques, but changing the material completely is prohibited.","The act's introduction is optional. If you introduce yourself, the time counts as part of your performance time (District 11).","District 5/4: each act is introduced by the announcer just before the performance, using the description in the Required Information Form. Anything you add counts against your performance time.","District 5/4: there is no place to warm up or practice. A short time to view the stage and backstage is allowed after participant orientation.","District 5/4: male and female dressing rooms are provided.","District 11: an audience of participants, parents and guests may be in the contest room as far as the room allows. Audience members may only come and go between performances and must give their full attention and respect to each act."]},{Key:"eligibility",Title:"Who Can Enter",Items:["Entries are for 4-H members. Age divisions are Junior, Intermediate and Senior; teams are made up of members of the same age division (District 5/4).","The documents do not print the ages of the divisions.","District 11: a member may enter one Group One category and one Group Two category.","Group One: Choreographed Routines, Variety Show, Instrumental Music, Vocal. Group Two: 4-H Skit, Poetry/Prose, Solo/Band Performance. The groups match the Wednesday and Thursday contest days of State Round-Up for senior members who advance.","District 11: an entry has 1 to 9 participants.","District 5/4: enter as an individual and/or as a team of 2 to 9 members.","District 5/4: each county may enter two contestants or teams per age division per category.","County Extension Agents are strongly encouraged to review entries for the correct category, suitable material and compliance with all rules."]},{Key:"registration",Title:"How to Register",Items:["District 11: register on 4-H online and select the correct category.","District 5/4: complete the Required Information Form and give it to your county Extension agent by {{InfoFormDeadline}}. Form: {{InfoFormLink}}.","District 5/4: the act's introduction and any music required are submitted on the Required Information Form.","District 11: to use the Bluetooth speaker provided in the contest room, submit your music by {{MusicUploadDeadline}} as an mp3, mp4 or wav file to the folder {{MusicUploadFolder}}. The document also says the files are due no later than April 25 and April 26, so upload by the earliest date.","Name the music file with your name, county and category, for example Jane Doe Lavaca Choreographed Routine. There is one folder for Choreographed Routine and one for Vocal.","If you do not submit music by the deadline, you must bring your own speaker and device (District 11)."]},{Key:"levels",Title:"Contest Levels",Items:["The contest runs at county, district and state level.","The first, second and third place winners in each category at the county contest qualify for the district contest (District 11).","At District 5/4 the finals are the Come Alive event, where each act is introduced by the announcer."]},{Key:"conduct",Title:"Props, Equipment and Conduct",Items:["Props must go through doors 6 feet wide and 7 feet tall.","District 11: space is limited. Each entry may bring props that fit in a space 3 feet by 8 feet.","District 11: one Bluetooth speaker and one microphone with a stand are provided in each contest room that needs music. A piano is available for Instrumental Music. All other props and equipment, such as music stands and stools, must be brought by the participants.","District 11: contestants compete in an open ballroom with a carpeted floor. Choreographed routine and skit participants should prepare for a space smaller than 20 by 30 feet.","District 5/4: a piano is not available. Contestants must bring their own keyboard if needed.","District 5/4: bring a device (smartphone, CD player, MP3 player, laptop) with a 1/4 inch aux connection for the PA system. Speakers and input cable are provided. A projector is not provided.","District 5/4: the stage is {{StageSize}}.","Only adult coaches and agents may be backstage, near the prop storage area, and help with set-up and break-down. Other 4-H members or youth who are not part of the team may not help.","District 5/4: one person from the group should work with the stage manager at set-up and know where every item goes.","During a performance adult coaches may give music cues and help with costume or prop changes backstage. They may not take part in any other way. Any voice heard from backstage must be a participant or a recorded voice.","No accompanist is permitted in any category. If music is needed, it must be recorded or performed by the contestant."]},{Key:"judging",Title:"Time Limits and Judging",Items:["All categories have 4 minutes for set-up and break-down and a maximum of 6 minutes for presentation, 10 minutes in total per act. Time limits are strictly enforced.","A penalty of 5 points per minute, or part of a minute, over the time limit is deducted from the total score.","Judges decide whether an entry is in the correct category. A wrong category may mean disqualification.","Marks for each criterion are not printed in the district documents. See the score cards at {{StateGuidelinesLink}}."]},{Key:"other",Title:"Prohibited Items",Items:["These may not be used in any category: talcum or baby powder, flour, pies, food (District 5/4), water, oil, loose feathers, flower petals, hay, straw, helium balloons, glitter, sand, confetti, open flames, or other substances that are hard to clean up, may cause damage or are dangerous.","No roller skates, shoes with spikes, cleats, motorized vehicles or live animals.","District 11: no real firearms. A prop that looks like a firearm needs prior approval from the contest directors, {{StageContact}} or {{VocalContact}}."]}],Documents:[{Title:"District 11 Talent Show Case guidelines 2025-26",Url:"https://d114-h.tamu.edu/files/2025/12/2025-2026-Talent-Show-Case-D-11-Guidelines.pdf"},{Title:"District 5/4 Talent Showcase rules 2023",Url:"https://d54-h.tamu.edu/files/2023/01/2023-Talent-Showcase-Rules-Guidelines-1.pdf"},{Title:"Texas 4-H Roundup state guidelines",Url:"https://texas4-h.tamu.edu/events/roundup/"}]},o=[{ParticipantType:"Individual",Source:"District 5/4 rules (2023), Entry",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["An individual may enter. District 11 treats a single member as an entry of 1 participant.","In Solo/Band Performance, a solo performer must play an instrument and sing."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- An individual may enter. District 11 treats a single member as an entry of 1 participant.
- In Solo/Band Performance, a solo performer must play an instrument and sing.`},{ParticipantType:"Team",Source:"District 5/4 rules (2023), Entry; District 11 guidelines (rev. 17 Nov 2025)",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["A team has 2 to 9 members (District 5/4). District 11 allows 1 to 9 participants per entry.","Team members must be in the same age division.","All 4-H members entered must be part of the act in every category."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- A team has 2 to 9 members (District 5/4). District 11 allows 1 to 9 participants per entry.
- Team members must be in the same age division.
- All 4-H members entered must be part of the act in every category.`}],a=[],i=JSON.parse('[{"Title":"Choreographed Routines","Source":"District 11 guidelines (rev. 17 Nov 2025), category 2; District 5/4 rules (2023)","Sections":{"About":["The act requires choreography: twirling, pom pom squad routines, jump rope teams, basketball dribbling exhibitions, or dance (jazz, tap, country and western, ballroom and others). Group One."],"TimeAndFormat":["Set-up and break-down 4 minutes; presentation up to 6 minutes; 10 minutes in total."],"Rules":["No speaking to form a skit or story line.","Sign language presentations to music are included. If a participant is singing and signing, enter the Vocal category.","All 4-H members entered must be part of the act."],"Allowed":["Recorded music on a CD or digital music player."],"NotAllowed":["An accompanist."],"Judging":["Judged on material chosen, talent, uniformity (District 11), creativity, showmanship and costuming."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The act requires choreography: twirling, pom pom squad routines, jump rope teams, basketball dribbling exhibitions, or dance (jazz, tap, country and western, ballroom and others). Group One.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Set-up and break-down 4 minutes; presentation up to 6 minutes; 10 minutes in total.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- No speaking to form a skit or story line.\\n- Sign language presentations to music are included. If a participant is singing and signing, enter the Vocal category.\\n- All 4-H members entered must be part of the act.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Recorded music on a CD or digital music player.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- An accompanist.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged on material chosen, talent, uniformity (District 11), creativity, showmanship and costuming."},{"Title":"Variety Show","Source":"District 11 guidelines (rev. 17 Nov 2025), category 3; District 5/4 rules (2023)","Sections":{"About":["An acting category of variety entertainment: sketch comedy, magic, acrobatics, juggling, ventriloquism and other acts that do not fit the other six categories. Group One."],"TimeAndFormat":["Set-up and break-down 4 minutes; presentation up to 6 minutes; 10 minutes in total."],"Rules":["No 4-H related material or theme. Otherwise the act is a 4-H Skit.","Creativity is encouraged, but degrading any individual or organization is not permitted.","Music, vocal selections and choreography may be used, but not more than half of the performance."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judged on material chosen, talent, creativity, showmanship, costumes and props."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- An acting category of variety entertainment: sketch comedy, magic, acrobatics, juggling, ventriloquism and other acts that do not fit the other six categories. Group One.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Set-up and break-down 4 minutes; presentation up to 6 minutes; 10 minutes in total.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- No 4-H related material or theme. Otherwise the act is a 4-H Skit.\\n- Creativity is encouraged, but degrading any individual or organization is not permitted.\\n- Music, vocal selections and choreography may be used, but not more than half of the performance.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged on material chosen, talent, creativity, showmanship, costumes and props."},{"Title":"Instrumental Music","Source":"District 11 guidelines (rev. 17 Nov 2025), category 4; District 5/4 rules (2023) (Musical/Instrumental)","Sections":{"About":["A musical presentation with instruments, accompanied by background recorded music or instruments only. Group One."],"TimeAndFormat":["Set-up and break-down 4 minutes; presentation up to 6 minutes; 10 minutes in total."],"Rules":["Participants may not sing or add a skit, poetry, prose or choreography.","A piano is provided at District 11 but not at District 5/4, where contestants bring their own keyboard."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["An accompanist."],"Judging":["Judged on talent, showmanship, musical presentation and material chosen."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- A musical presentation with instruments, accompanied by background recorded music or instruments only. Group One.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Set-up and break-down 4 minutes; presentation up to 6 minutes; 10 minutes in total.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Participants may not sing or add a skit, poetry, prose or choreography.\\n- A piano is provided at District 11 but not at District 5/4, where contestants bring their own keyboard.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- An accompanist.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged on talent, showmanship, musical presentation and material chosen."},{"Title":"Vocal","Source":"District 11 guidelines (rev. 17 Nov 2025), category 6; District 5/4 rules (2023)","Sections":{"About":["A vocal presentation, a cappella or with an accompaniment recording. Group One."],"TimeAndFormat":["Set-up and break-down 4 minutes; presentation up to 6 minutes; 10 minutes in total."],"Rules":["All members in the act must be singing.","Singers may move around the stage and use choreography to improve showmanship.","Sign language may be added, but an entry that is only sign language without singing must be entered in Choreographed Routines."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["An accompanist.","Lip sync.","Playing an instrument.","Skits, poetry or other speaking during the act."],"Judging":["Judged on talent, showmanship, vocal presentation and material chosen."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- A vocal presentation, a cappella or with an accompaniment recording. Group One.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Set-up and break-down 4 minutes; presentation up to 6 minutes; 10 minutes in total.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- All members in the act must be singing.\\n- Singers may move around the stage and use choreography to improve showmanship.\\n- Sign language may be added, but an entry that is only sign language without singing must be entered in Choreographed Routines.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- An accompanist.\\n- Lip sync.\\n- Playing an instrument.\\n- Skits, poetry or other speaking during the act.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged on talent, showmanship, vocal presentation and material chosen."},{"Title":"4-H Skit","Source":"District 11 guidelines (rev. 17 Nov 2025), category 1; District 5/4 rules (2023)","Sections":{"About":["A skit with a 4-H based story line, promoting 4-H, community service, a project or an activity, or addressing a youth issue and how 4-H efforts can help. Group Two."],"TimeAndFormat":["Set-up and break-down 4 minutes; presentation up to 6 minutes; 10 minutes in total."],"Rules":["Music, vocal selections and choreography may be used through dialogue and story, but not more than half of the performance.","A skit may be humorous and make fun of, but not degrade, Extension employees or the 4-H program.","All 4-H members entered must be part of the act."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judged on material chosen, talent, creativity, showmanship, costumes and props."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- A skit with a 4-H based story line, promoting 4-H, community service, a project or an activity, or addressing a youth issue and how 4-H efforts can help. Group Two.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Set-up and break-down 4 minutes; presentation up to 6 minutes; 10 minutes in total.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Music, vocal selections and choreography may be used through dialogue and story, but not more than half of the performance.\\n- A skit may be humorous and make fun of, but not degrade, Extension employees or the 4-H program.\\n- All 4-H members entered must be part of the act.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged on material chosen, talent, creativity, showmanship, costumes and props."},{"Title":"Poetry/Prose","Source":"District 11 guidelines (rev. 17 Nov 2025), category 5; District 5/4 rules (2023)","Sections":{"About":["An act that showcases poetry or prose. Group Two. Poetry is generally structured meter and rhyme that tells a story or gives a message. Prose has more variety of rhythm and is closer to everyday speech; it can be an excerpt from a larger piece such as a play or book."],"TimeAndFormat":["Set-up and break-down 4 minutes; presentation up to 6 minutes; 10 minutes in total."],"Rules":["4-H related material is not required. An original poem or prose piece about 4-H is acceptable.","Every member entered must take part on stage.","All material must be memorized. No script may be used (District 5/4)."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Vocal, musical or choreographed routines in the act."],"Judging":["Judged on material chosen, message, talent, presentation, style and props or costuming."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- An act that showcases poetry or prose. Group Two. Poetry is generally structured meter and rhyme that tells a story or gives a message. Prose has more variety of rhythm and is closer to everyday speech; it can be an excerpt from a larger piece such as a play or book.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Set-up and break-down 4 minutes; presentation up to 6 minutes; 10 minutes in total.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- 4-H related material is not required. An original poem or prose piece about 4-H is acceptable.\\n- Every member entered must take part on stage.\\n- All material must be memorized. No script may be used (District 5/4).\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Vocal, musical or choreographed routines in the act.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged on material chosen, message, talent, presentation, style and props or costuming."},{"Title":"Solo/Band Performance","Source":"District 11 guidelines (rev. 17 Nov 2025), category 7; District 5/4 rules (2023)","Sections":{"About":["An act that combines vocal and instrumental talent. Group Two. Acts that are vocal only or instrumental only must not be entered here."],"TimeAndFormat":["Set-up and break-down 4 minutes; presentation up to 6 minutes; 10 minutes in total."],"Rules":["Every member must play an instrument, sing, or both. A solo performer must play an instrument and sing.","Singing must be part of the act.","Members may move around the stage and use choreography to improve showmanship.","A piano is not available at District 5/4; bring your own keyboard."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Skits, poetry or prose."],"Judging":["Judged on talent, showmanship, musical presentation, vocal presentation when applicable, and material chosen."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- An act that combines vocal and instrumental talent. Group Two. Acts that are vocal only or instrumental only must not be entered here.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Set-up and break-down 4 minutes; presentation up to 6 minutes; 10 minutes in total.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Every member must play an instrument, sing, or both. A solo performer must play an instrument and sing.\\n- Singing must be part of the act.\\n- Members may move around the stage and use choreography to improve showmanship.\\n- A piano is not available at District 5/4; bring your own keyboard.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Skits, poetry or prose.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged on talent, showmanship, musical presentation, vocal presentation when applicable, and material chosen."}]'),r=[],s=[{Key:"MusicUploadDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Last date to upload music (District 11)",Value:"2026-04-24",Source:"District 11 guidelines (rev. 17 Nov 2025), Equipment (printed April 24, 2026; the text also says April 25 and April 26)"},{Key:"MusicUploadFolder",Kind:"link",Label:"Music upload folder (District 11)",Value:"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1Bde-hLrcGH7NJDrCsqRmIe-0FD2wiDWf?usp=drive_link",Source:"District 11 guidelines (rev. 17 Nov 2025), Equipment"},{Key:"InfoFormDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Last date for the Required Information Form (District 5/4, 2023 edition)",Value:"March 31",Source:"District 5/4 rules (2023), Required Information Form"},{Key:"InfoFormLink",Kind:"link",Label:"Required Information Form (District 5/4, 2023 edition)",Value:"https://agrilife.org/d54h/files/2023/01/2023-Talent-Showcase-Information-Sheet.pdf",Source:"District 5/4 rules (2023)"},{Key:"StateGuidelinesLink",Kind:"link",Label:"Texas 4-H Roundup state guidelines and scorecards",Value:"https://texas4-h.tamu.edu/events/roundup/",Source:"District 11 guidelines (rev. 17 Nov 2025), Rules"},{Key:"StageSize",Kind:"text",Label:"Stage area (District 5/4, 2023 edition)",Value:"about 10 feet wide and 10 feet deep and raised, with projector screen, stool, table, chair and theatrical lighting (no spotlights)",Source:"District 5/4 rules (2023), Stage Contest Area"},{Key:"VocalContact",Kind:"contact",Label:"Contact: Contest director: Vocal, Instrumental Music and Solo/Band Performance questions",Value:{Name:"Michelle Wright",Role:"Contest director: Vocal, Instrumental Music and Solo/Band Performance questions",Phone:"979-865-2078",WhatsApp:"",Email:"michelle.wright@ag.tamu.edu"},Source:"District 11 guidelines (rev. 17 Nov 2025), Rules"},{Key:"StageContact",Kind:"contact",Label:"Contact: Contest director: Choreographed Routines, Variety Show, 4-H Skit, Poetry/Prose and music upload questions",Value:{Name:"Natalie Knesek",Role:"Contest director: Choreographed Routines, Variety Show, 4-H Skit, Poetry/Prose and music upload questions",Phone:"361-798-2221",WhatsApp:"",Email:"natalie.knesek@ag.tamu.edu"},Source:"District 11 guidelines (rev. 17 Nov 2025), Rules and Equipment"}],l=[{Claim:"Rules and categories are as printed by Texas 4-H District 11 (2025-26) and District 5/4 (2023).",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"District 11 Talent Show Case guidelines",Url:"https://d114-h.tamu.edu/files/2025/12/2025-2026-Talent-Show-Case-D-11-Guidelines.pdf"},{Claim:"Entry limits, team sizes, county caps and the Required Information Form are from the District 5/4 rules.",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"District 5/4 Talent Showcase rules",Url:"https://d54-h.tamu.edu/files/2023/01/2023-Talent-Showcase-Rules-Guidelines-1.pdf"}],c={TemplateKey:e,Year:2026,Note:t,Page:n,ParticipantTypes:o,AgeGroups:a,Competitions:i,CompetitionAgeGroups:r,Variables:s,Evidence:l};export{a as AgeGroups,r as CompetitionAgeGroups,i as Competitions,l as Evidence,t as Note,n as Page,o as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,s as Variables,u as Year,c as default};
